  "body": "### Summary\nAs the operator, I want to decide whether the super-favourite row keeps its old tint in dark mode and with Increase Contrast, because #576 made it stronger there while its PR and code comment say the look did not change.\n\nRefs #576 (found in its Mac check).\n\n### Observed\n#576 replaced `Color.orange.opacity(0.12)` with `RowTint(tint: .orange, base: .clear)`, whose strength is the unread-MP rule. The strength is no longer 0.12:\n\n| Setting | Before | After | Measured row (iPad, after) | Visible change |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Light | 0.12 | 0.10 | 243,232,226 | none to the eye |\n| Dark | 0.12 | 0.16 | 41,23,8 | stronger |\n| Increase Contrast, light | 0.12 | 0.18 | 228,208,197 | stronger |\n| Increase Contrast, dark | 0.12 | 0.24 | 61,38,21 | stronger |\n\nThe \"before\" column comes from the diff of #576; no pre-#576 build was run side by side. Build 4b1e77f5, iPad Pro 13-inch (M5) simulator, iOS 27.0. No grey card; the selected row steps aside as intended.\n\n`TopicListView.superFavoriteTint`'s comment says \"the row looked like this before\", which holds only in light.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- Decision: keep the shared strength (update the comment and GAP-227) or restore 0.12 for super-favourites. #572 owns the state-tint definition.\n",
